# Line endings are forced to LF on checkout, on every platform, regardless
# of `core.autocrlf`. Without this, Windows checks text files out with CRLF
# by default — including `tests/fixtures/logo.svg` and every `.rs` file's own
# raw-string fixtures — which breaks every byte-identical comparison the
# project's determinism invariants depend on (AGENTS.md invariants 1 and 2)
# purely because of how the file happened to be checked out, not because of
# anything Shaipe did.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never touched: normalizing line endings in a binary asset corrupts it.
# `text=auto`'s own detection should already skip these, but a font or an
# image is exactly the kind of file where "should" is not good enough.
*.png binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico binary
